fixed: ["'Your use' table, Elite 100 V2 row: replaced 'a quiet fan' with '30 dB at loads under 600 W (BLUETTI), noticeably louder in Turbo mode (Notebookcheck)' and kept '1,000 W solar input'. BLUETTI's page (read 2026-11-15) says 'The Elite 100 V2 operates at only 30dB under 600W' and does not name a Silent mode. Notebookcheck (Christian Hintze, read 2026-11-15) says the under-30 dB claim 'only applies in Silent mode', which limits power to 600 W, and that 'In Turbo mode... the unit becomes noticeably louder.' Updated the BLUETTI and Notebookcheck source labels to match.", "The same wrong claim was in the Elite's buy sentence ('want a quiet fan'). Changed it to 'keep loads under 600 W when they want it quiet', based on the same two sources.", "The requested claim that the Elite has the lowest cost per usable Wh is false on this page's own figures, so I did not write it. The DJI Power 1000 V2 is $399.98 on Amazon (amzcheck, ASIN B0H2MFBDZL, read 2026-11-15), and $399.98 ÷ 880 Wh = $0.45, below the Elite's $499 (BLUETTI store, read 2026-11-15) ÷ 890 Wh = $0.56. The DELTA 3 is $579 on the EcoFlow US store (storecheck search, read 2026-11-15), and $579 ÷ 870 Wh = $0.67; added that source.", "Changed the Elite-only cost bullet into a cost-per-usable-Wh bullet for the three stations whose price I read today: DJI $0.45, Elite $0.56, DELTA 3 $0.67. Added one after-section sentence that says what the Elite wins on the page's figures: the highest rated solar input of the five (1,000 W). The 
